`npm run production` fails on webpack 5.106.2 because `ProgressPlugin._applyOnCompiler()` now validates `this.options` during compilation (via `compiler.hooks.validate`). `webpackbar` 5.x overwrites `this.options` after calling `super()`, exposing properties (`name`, `color`, `reporters`, `reporter`) that are not in webpack's `ProgressPlugin` schema:

```js
// webpackbar 5.x — breaks with webpack 5.106+
constructor(options) {
    super({ activeModules: true }); // sets this.options = { activeModules: true } ✓
    this.options = Object.assign({}, DEFAULTS, options); // overwrites with { name, color, reporters, reporter } ✗
}

// webpackbar 7.x — keeps this.options valid
constructor(options) {
    super({ activeModules: true, handler: ... }); // this.options stays valid ✓
    this.webpackbar = new WebpackBar(options);     // custom config in separate class
}
```

## Changes

- **`package.json`**: Add `"webpackbar": "^7.0.0"` to `overrides` so npm forces v7 in place of the v5 transitive dependency pulled in by `laravel-mix`
- **`package-lock.json`**: Updated to reflect webpackbar 7.0.0
